                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">WFM T–10 (Supplement)</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Views of the Embassy in London on Probable British
                        Attitudes on Subjects To Be Discussed in the Washington Foreign Ministers’
                        Meetings</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">korea (if armistice)</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The British fear that Korea may fall to the Communists by political means, and
                    they may suggest general talks outside UN in order to facilitate Chinese
                    Communist participation, preferably limited to Korea but in any event with Korea
                    as first agenda item and agreement on other subjects dependent upon reaching an
                    agreement on Korea.</p>
            </div>
